  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Palestine: Judicial Training on Commercial Law</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To provide relevant Palestinian authorities, including the High Judicial Council (HJC) and the Palestinian Judicial Institute (PJI), with high-standard judicial training on commercial law issues, with focus on negotiable commercial instruments, bankruptcy and insolvency, selected commercial contracts, banking transactions, and commercial act and disputes. 2) To develop e-learning modules for the delivered trainings. 3) To monitor the improvement of participants&apos; knowledge.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The High Judicial Council (HJC) and the Palestinian Judicial Institute (PJI).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to enhance the capacity of Palestinian judges to deal more effectively with commercial law matters, by providing substantive training on commercial law issues.</narrative>
  </description>
